{"name":"Truth","hex":"#344989","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Truth","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An entry posted on the Truth Social platform. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Truth"}],"entries":[{"title":"Truth","blocks":[{"text":"Truth is commonly understood as conformity to reality or fact. It contrasts with falsity or misrepresentation that fails to align with the world. Truth is typically treated as a property of sentences, propositions, or beliefs that describe things as they are. It is closely related to truthfulness, a virtue associated with honesty, and to truthlikeness, a characteristic of theories that approximate the truth."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truth"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Alfred_Tarski_1968_%28as-is%2C_cropped%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alfred Tarski formulated the semantic theory of truth.[43]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlfred_Tarski_1968_(as-is%2C_cropped)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/What_is_truth.jpg/500px-What_is_truth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb